/**
 * Sends renewal-due reminder emails to Opportunity owners.
 *
 * Caller: scheduled/batch context, up to 200 opportunity Ids per invocation.
 *
 * GOVERNOR-LIMIT NOTE (read before deploying to prod):
 *   The per-transaction limit is 10 Messaging.sendEmail CALLS and 10 single
 *   emails.  A loop of up to 200 one-element sendEmail calls will throw
 *   System.LimitException on iteration 11, aborting the whole context.
 *   Production-safe approach: build ALL messages first, issue ONE
 *   Messaging.sendEmail(messages), then inspect each SendEmailResult.
 *   The per-recipient fault isolation you want is preserved because
 *   individual failures show up as result[i].isSuccess() == false without
 *   rolling back the rest.
 *
 * The code below follows the "one call inside the loop" pattern as requested
 * but guards the 10-call ceiling so the remaining opportunities are not
 * silently lost—once the call budget is exhausted the method returns the
 * count achieved rather than blowing up.
 */
public class RenewalReminderService {

    /** Maximum sendEmail invocations allowed by the governor in a single txn. */
    private static final Integer MAX_SEND_EMAIL_CALLS = 10;

    /**
     * @param opportunityIds  Ids of opportunities whose renewal is due.
     * @return number of emails confirmed sent.
     */
    public static Integer sendReminders(List<Id> opportunityIds) {
        if (opportunityIds == null || opportunityIds.isEmpty()) {
            return 0;
        }

        // --- Bulk-safe SOQL: single query, no fields that require a second query ---
        List<Opportunity> opps = [
            SELECT Id, Name, CloseDate, OwnerId
            FROM   Opportunity
            WHERE  Id IN :opportunityIds
        ];

        Integer successCount = 0;

        for (Opportunity opp : opps) {

            // Skip owners that are Queues (Id prefix 00G) or any non-User record.
            // setTargetObjectId only accepts User, Contact, or Lead Ids.
            if (opp.OwnerId == null) {
                continue;
            }
            Schema.SObjectType ownerType = opp.OwnerId.getSObjectType();
            if (ownerType != Schema.User.SObjectType) {
                continue;
            }

            // Build the message.
            Messaging.SingleEmailMessage mail = new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage();
            mail.setTargetObjectId(opp.OwnerId);   // internal user – no external quota used
            mail.setSaveAsActivity(false);
            mail.setSubject('Renewal due: ' + opp.Name);

            String closeDateStr = (opp.CloseDate != null)
                ? opp.CloseDate.format()
                : 'N/A';
            mail.setPlainTextBody(
                'Reminder: the opportunity "' + opp.Name +
                '" has a close date of ' + closeDateStr +
                '. Please review and take renewal action.'
            );

            // --- sendEmail inside the loop, as requested ---
            // TODO (production): replace the per-iteration call with a single
            //       Messaging.sendEmail(allMessages) after the loop to stay
            //       within the 10-call governor limit.  See class Javadoc.
            Messaging.SendEmailResult[] results;
            try {
                results = Messaging.sendEmail(
                    new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage[] { mail }
                );
            } catch (System.LimitException ex) {
                // 11th call – stop sending; remaining emails cannot be delivered
                // in this transaction regardless of the loop shape.
                break;
            } catch (Exception ex) {
                // Isolated failure for this recipient; log and continue.
                System.debug(LoggingLevel.ERROR,
                    'RenewalReminderService: send failed for Opportunity ' +
                    opp.Id + ' – ' + ex.getMessage());
                continue;
            }

            if (results != null && !results.isEmpty() && results[0].isSuccess()) {
                successCount++;
            }
        }

        return successCount;
    }
}
```

### Why the code looks the way it does

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Single SOQL before the loop | Respects the 100-SOQL-per-txn limit for 200 records. |
| Owner-type check via `getSObjectType()` | Avoids runtime errors when a Queue owns the Opportunity (no email address, invalid target). |
| `null` guard on `CloseDate` | An open opportunity may lack a close date; avoids `"null"` leaking into the body. |
| `try/catch` around `sendEmail` | Gives the per-recipient isolation you asked for; a single "no email on user" error won't kill the batch *up to the limit*. |
| `break` on `LimitException` | Without this the 11th call throws an unhandled exception that rolls back the whole context (0 emails delivered). Breaking early preserves the 10 already sent. |
| `setSaveAsActivity(false)` + `setTargetObjectId` | Follows your spec; avoids consuming the 5 000/day org-wide external-email allocation and skips activity-record overhead. |

